<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to auction 7-yr bonds of HUF5bln on Feb 13.</title>
<headline>Hungary to auction 7-yr bonds of HUF5bln on Feb 13.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction five billion forint worth of the seven-year government bonds of 2003/F series on February 13, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    Date of issue		17 October 1996</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   24 September 2003</p>
<p>    Bills on offer	     5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Minimum net price	  102.92 pct</p>
<p>Average price at last</p>
<p>	 auction (Jan 16)	103.42 pct</p>
<p>NOTE -  The bond bears a floating interest, calculated on March 20 and September 20 every year adding three percent to year-on-year consumer inflation. The interest is paid once a year, on September 24. The starting interest is 25.9 percent.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
